  - m_Id: 2361805377536
    m_Localized: HOW TO PLAY L-PROJECT
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2738785226752
    m_Localized: "<size=150%><b>COMPONENTS</b>\r</size>\n-    32 white puzzle\rs\n-   
      20 black puzzle\rs\n-    90 pieces (10x each of the 9 shapes)\r\n\r\n\n<size=150%><b>GAMEPLAY
      OVERVIEW\r</b>\r</size>\nIn Project L, you complete puzzles with your pieces
      to earn as many points as you can to win the game.\n\n\n<size=120%><b>PIECES\r</b>\r</size>\nEach
      player starts with just two pieces. During the game, you build your supply
      of pieces so you can complete increasingly difficult puzzles and earn plenty
      of points.\n\n\n<size=120%><b>PUZZLES\r</b>\r</size>\nA puzzle is complited
      when you fill its recessed area with your pieces. After that, take all you
      pieces back, place the puzzle aside, and reap the rewards: points and a new
      piece.\n\n\n<size=150%><b>SETUP\r</b>\r</size>\n-    Take all the white puzzles
      and create a white puzzle deck. Then create a black puzzle deck according to
      the table below:\r\n    |--------------------------------------|----|----|----|\n   
      |Number of Players:               |  2 |  3 |  4 |\n    |Black puzzles:                      
      | 12| 14| 16|\n    |--------------------------------------|----|----|----|\n-   
      Put both decks in the middle of the table face down and place four puzzles
      from each deck face up in a row next to it.\r\n-    Create a reserve of pieces
      in reach of all players.\r\n-    Give every player a level-1 piece and a level-2
      piece to start with.\r\n\r\n\n<size=150%><b>GAMEPLAY</b>\r</size>\nStarting
      with the first player, players take turns in a clockwise order. On your turn,
      you can do three actions (you can repeate actions until you do a total of three):\r\n-   
      <b>Take a puzzle</b> from one of the rows and place it in front of you. Then
      replace the puzzle you took from the row with another one from the corresponding
      puzzle deck. You can have a maximum of 4 unfinished puzzles in front of you
      at the same time.\r\n-    <b>Take a level-1 piece</b>,from the reserve and
      place it into your supply.\r\n-    <b>Upgrade a piece</b> in your supply 1
      level up (return the original piece to the reserve and take another piece that
      is 1 level higher).\r\n       - If there are no pieces in the reserve that
      are 1 level higher (no matter what shape), skip to the next available level.\r\n      
      - Instead of upgrading to a higher level piece, you may exchange your piece
      for one that is the same level (a different shape) or lower.\r\n-    <b>Place
      a piece on one of your puzzles.</b> You can flip or rotate the piece so it
      fits into the recessed area and doesn't overlap with other pieces. You cannot
      move or take back a piece from a puzzle until you complete that puzzle (see
      Completing Puzzles).\r\n-    <b>Master Action</b> (once per round) Place up
      to one piece on each puzzle in front of you. All pieces you wish to place must
      be in your supply at the start of this action.\r\n\r\n\n<size=150%><b>COMPLETING
      PUZZLES</b>\r</size>\nA puzzle is completed once its recessed area is filled
      with pieces. After you finish the action that let you complete a puzzle:\r\n-   
      Take all the pieces from the puzzle bak into your supply (you can use them
      again).\r\n-    Place the puzzle face up, apart from your unfinished puzzles,
      to create a victory point pile showing how many points you have earned.\r\n-   
      Get the reward on the puzzle (a new piece from the reserve into your supply).\r\n\r\n\n<size=150%><b>END
      GAME\r</b>\r</size>\nThe endgame triggers once the black puzzle deck runs out
      (there will still be four black puzzles available in the row when this happens).
      Finish the current round so that everyone has played the same number of turns.
      After that, play one final round.\r\n\n\n<size=150%><b>FINISHEING TOUCHES\r</b>\r</size>\nAfter
      the final round ends, all players may perform Finishing Touches on the puzzles
      in front of them that they didn't complete during the game:\r\n-    Place any
      number of pieces from your supply on the puzzles in front of you. For each
      piece you place this way, deduct 1 point from your final score.\r\n-    When
      you are done with all your Finishing Touches, put the puzzles you have completed
      on your victory point pile (but do not collect any additional rewards).\r\n\r\n\n<size=150%><b>FINAL
      SCORING</b>\r</size>\nCount the pints on all the puzzles in your victory point
      pile and deduct point for any Finishing Touches you made. The player with the
      most points wins the game.\r\n-    In case of a tie, the player who has completed
      more puzzles wins.\r\n-    If there is still a tie, the player with more pieces
      wins.\r\n-    If there is still a tie, all tied players share the victory.
      You are all awesome!\r\n"
